# ⚠ WITHOUT THIS FILE, `COPY . .` SHIPS THE HOST'S node_modules INTO THE IMAGE.
#
# Every app Dockerfile installs dependencies in an earlier stage and then does
# `COPY . .` for the sources. With no ignore file that copy also brings whatever
# node_modules the machine running the build happens to have — on a Mac that
# means darwin-arm64 binaries landing in a linux image, and pnpm noticing the
# store no longer matches and trying to purge node_modules mid-build:
#
#   ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY
#
# CI never hit it because a fresh checkout has no node_modules — which is worse,
# not better: it means local builds and CI builds were producing different
# images from the same commit.

# Installed in the image, never copied in.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, produced in the image.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.astro
**/.astro
.turbo
**/.turbo
apps/docs/.nimbus

# Vendored at build time by apps/docs/scripts/vendor-scalar.mjs — 8.8 MB that
# would otherwise be sent to the daemon on every build.
apps/docs/public/scalar

# Never belongs in an image.
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Noise in the build context.
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage
**/coverage
